surname>Burge</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wedzicha</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>COPD exacerbations: definitions and classifications</article-title><source>Eur Respir J</source><year>2003</year><volume>21</volume><issue>Suppl 4</issue><fpage>46S</fpage><lpage>53S</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-copd-5-041"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miravitlles</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayordomo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Artes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and its exacerbations in general practice</article-title><source>Respir Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10464874</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-copd-5-041"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Decramer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Celli</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kesten</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effects of tiotropium on outcomes in GOLD stage II COPD: Subgroup analysis from the UPLIFT (Understanding Potential Long-term Impacts on Function with Tiotropium) Study</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2009</year><volume>374</volume><fpage>1171</fpage><lpage>1178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19716598</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-copd-5-041"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O&#x02019;Reilly</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><n